# Voice and copy

## Hard bans

- No em dashes (`—`) or en dashes used as clause breaks. Use commas, periods, colons, or parentheses.
- No obvious AI filler: "delve", "seamless", "robust", "leverage", "cutting-edge", "elevate", "empower", "unlock", "in today's world", "it's important to note".
- No stacked marketing cadence: short hype line, short hype line, short hype line.
- No unnecessary Capitalization Of Every Word in headings, buttons, or labels.
- No fake enthusiasm or empty superlatives in UI strings, README blurbs, or error messages.

## Preferred voice

- Plain, specific, product-true. Say what the screen does.
- Sentence case for headings and buttons ("Send to Mobile Money", not "Send To Mobile Money").
- Prefer "Bitcoin received" / "RWF delivered" over vague "Success!" / "All set!".
- Direct, Rwanda-first, fee-transparent. Do not invent a brand voice.

## Examples

```
Bad:  Making Stablecoins Spendable — Instantly & Seamlessly
Good: Making stablecoins spendable

Bad:  Unlock Your Lightning-Powered Offramp Experience
Good: Pay with Lightning. Get RWF on MoMo.

Bad:  Something went wrong — please try again later!
Good: Payment could not be sent. Check the number and try again.
```

## Docs and commits in this repo

Same rules. Keep AGENTS/docs factual. No decorative punctuation thrift-store (emoji showers, badge walls, "✨" fluff).
